# Env
# `.env*` is deliberately broad: `.env` + `.env.*` match only dot-separated
# variants, so a hand-named copy like `.env_from-praveen` stays UNIGNORED and
# `git add -A` would commit it. Matches the backend repo's rule. Do not narrow.
.env*
!.env.example
!.env.test

